Say whether startup.c is compiled at all

Runs 353 to 361 all agree: startup.c on disk carries nio_dc_puts("\nnio: HB ")
on line 456, the compile record names that file as the input, the object carries
_nio_heartbeat_thread -- and the object has no such literal, at 113,592 bytes
with links=1, byte-identical in every round.

Either the file is compiled and the literal vanishes (which no flag here
explains), or the object is written by something else and the file is never
compiled.  An #error in the file answers that in one round: a red build means
the compiler reached it, a green build means the object is not this file's
output.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/kern/startup.c b/osfmk/kern/startup.c
index 6127866..92cdae8 100644
--- a/osfmk/kern/startup.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/startup.c
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 #include <kern/boot_progress.h>
+#error nio-compile-detector-fired
